# Backend Architecture Rules

## Architectural style
- Respect Hexagonal / Clean / DDD boundaries already present in the codebase.
- Domain layer must not depend on infrastructure frameworks.
- Application layer orchestrates use-cases; domain contains business rules; infrastructure contains IO (DB, HTTP, messaging).

## Dependency direction
- domain -> (no deps on application/infrastructure)
- application -> domain
- infrastructure -> application/domain (adapters)

## Naming / Modularity
- Use domain language (ubiquitous language) for names.
- Keep modules cohesive; avoid "god services".

## Changes policy
- Prefer extending existing patterns over introducing new ones.
- If refactoring: keep behavior identical unless asked otherwise.
